      "nets": ["+3.3V", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "REG3's output is connected to the +3.3V net, while the FCC and NAVC MCU supply pins are connected to +3V3. The schematic shows no connection between these differently named nets.",
      "expected": "The regulator output and the MCU supply pins should share the same 3.3 V net so the MCUs receive power.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "REG3 LD39200PU33R, pin 1 OUT → +3.3V (Power sheet, page 1)"
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "FCC2 supply pins connect to +3V3 (Flight Control Computer sheet, page 2)"
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "NAVC2 supply pins connect to +3V3 (Navigation Computer sheet, page 3)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3.3 V LDO ... produces 3V3 for “MCUs and Sensors”"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Because +3.3V and +3V3 are distinct nets, the LDO output does not power the MCU supply pins on +3V3. The FCC and NAVC may fail to start, and their peripherals may be unavailable.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The regulator output is on +3.3V, but both MCU supply networks are labeled +3V3, with no connection shown between them. This leaves the MCUs disconnected from the specified 3.3 V regulator rail."
}

